description: Never weaken or salvage the local dev Postgres; benchmarks use a throwaway container
alwaysApply: true
---

# Dev database durability

The dev database container `monaco-postgres` (port 54322) keeps `fsync`, `synchronous_commit` and `full_page_writes` on. `docker-compose.yml` pins them on the command line.

- Never run `ALTER SYSTEM`, `pg_resetwal`, or any `fsync=off`, `synchronous_commit=off` or `full_page_writes=off` against it.
- Benchmarks and durability experiments run in a throwaway container on another port, removed afterwards: `docker run --rm -d --name bench-pg -p 54399:5432 -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=bench postgres:16-alpine -c fsync=off`.
- If the dev database will not start, stop and ask the user. The supported recovery is `just reset db`.

Why: on 2026-09-27 a benchmark left `fsync=off` persisted in the dev volume, the machine crashed, and Postgres came back with `PANIC: could not locate a valid checkpoint record`.
